SETI Astro Suite Pro
--------------------

TianWen builds on the source of SETI Astro Suite Pro by Franklin Marek, published
under the GNU General Public License version 3:

  https://github.com/setiastro/setiastrosuitepro

  Data: the sensor quantum-efficiency, filter-transmission and Pickles stellar
  spectrum curves of its `SASP_data.fits`, which `tools/import-sasp-data/` converts
  into TianWen's filter-curve and quantum-efficiency tables. The curves themselves
  come from their original publishers (sensor and filter vendors, the Pickles
  library) and keep those terms; the compilation is SETI Astro's.

  Method: several display and inference routines follow its published Python and
  say so where they do, among them the pivot1 background neutralisation, the
  StarStretch, statistical and generalised hyperbolic stretch curves, the border
  and stitching of tiled inference, and the test for an input already stretched.

GPL-3.0 material may be combined into an AGPL-3.0 work (AGPL-3.0 section 13). Its
AI model weights are licensed separately and are not used; see below.


External programs, invoked and never linked
-------------------------------------------

TianWen can drive several third-party programs as separate processes, passing data
through files and reading their output back. None of their code is compiled into
or distributed with TianWen, and each is obtained and licensed by the user
directly from its author:

  ASTAP (`AstapPlateSolver`)                 https://www.hnsky.org/astap.htm
  astrometry.net (`AstrometryNetPlateSolver`) https://astrometry.net
  GraXpert (gradient correction)             https://graxpert.com
  RC-Astro BlurXTerminator / NoiseXTerminator / StarXTerminator  https://www.rc-astro.com

**TianWen's own licence does not restrict driving these programs; each vendor's
terms govern its own software.** RC-Astro runs as a separate process
(`rc-astro --json`) against the user's own licence. GraXpert differs in one way:
TianWen does not run it, but loads its background-extraction model in process,
reading it where GraXpert put it and under GraXpert's own terms for its models.
TianWen distributes **no third-party model weights** and no vendor binaries of its
own; it locates what the user installed.
Nothing in this section forms part of TianWen's Corresponding Source, because none
of it is part of TianWen.

SETI Astro Suite Pro's ONNX models are no longer used at all. Since 2026-09-24
they carry their own licence (`COSMIC_CLARITY_LICENSE.txt`, on the release that
hosts them), which permits use only within SASpro, for personal non-commercial
processing, unless the author consents in writing. On 2026-09-26 TianWen stopped
loading them and stopped searching SASpro's models folder. Releases before that
read them only where SASpro or the user had put them, and never fetched or
redistributed them.

Building our own models meets a narrower restriction as well:
RC-Astro's licence forbids using its outputs to create, train, validate or
benchmark a competing model, naming paired input/output datasets explicitly. So
TianWen's own model work (docs/plans/ai-denoise-deconv.md) uses no RC-Astro or
SETI Astro output anywhere in its training, validation or metric path. SETI
Astro's licence, published since, forbids distilling its models or deriving new
ones from them, so that exclusion now holds on its own terms. Both prohibitions are
contractual rather than a matter of copyright, so TianWen's own
licence has no bearing on them either way.
